    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0251" n="247" xml:id="pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.76/71: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-22T15:00:00-05:00">January 22, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Reference your 16, January 20, 3 p.m. Department approves your action in
                    declining to ask the authorities of the British Concession to withdraw their
                    objection to the proposed installation.</p>
                <p>Repeat to the Embassy at Peiping and Hankow and to the Consulate General at
                    Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
